# Git, PR, review, merge (generic)
## Git
- Follow the repo's architecture, neighbouring code and its `.cursor/rules` / `AGENTS.md`.
- Own branch per task: `type/NN-short-slug` (issue number in the name, e.g. `fix/198-appexception-warning`; role prefix still fine if it includes `NN`). Never push to the default branch, never force-push; history rewrite only with owner approval.
- Minimal diff, implement to acceptance criteria. No libraries "just in case", no refactoring of neighbouring layers unless asked.
- Leave shared clones clean (default branch, no uncommitted changes).
## Tasks and PRs
- One issue = one owner = one PR (batch small related fixes). Status lives in the tracker (labels, board, review state), not in chat.
- **Canonical PR ↔ issue link (unless Dependabot):** branch includes `NN`; PR body `## Задача` with `#NN` only — never `closes`/`fix`/`fixes` before acceptance; immediately after opening (or before review) connect the PR in GitHub Development so the issue sidebar shows it (GraphQL / `gh` / branch from issue / `gh issue develop`). Lead verifies the Development link before merge; missing link = process bug to fix first. Dependabot: no issue link. Docs/process-only meta with no tracker task: «без задачи» (rare). Do not retrofit old closed issues.
- Post to chat only the PR link when ready, a blocker, or a decision question.
- Behaviour/API/contract/settings/infra change merges with the matching doc update.
## Review and CI
- CI is the gate: do not re-run locally what CI runs green; read failures from the job log, quote only failing lines.
- Review the diff, not the repo; comment only on problems.
- Depth by risk: trivial (docs, typos, trivial config) = CI + first-line review; normal code = CI + first-line review; risky (infra, CI, Docker/nginx, auth, data/migrations, secrets handling, runtime/network dependencies) = CI + first-line review + deeper security check.
- When the project enables Cursor Automations (`project-cursor-automations.mdc`), those comments are the first-line review; do not duplicate the same checklist in a second pass. Escalation rules live in `playbook-step-06-review.mdc`.
## Merge and deploy
- Merge only when all gates are met; only the designated merger merges. Before merge: Development link present (unless Dependabot / «без задачи»).
- Merge = deploy: one PR at a time; next merge only after the previous deploy is green.
- Dependencies (Dependabot, minor, patch, and major): squash-merge without a separate owner yes when CI is green and nothing needs the owner's clarification. Treat a peer conflict, red CI, or an unclear breaking change as needing clarification. After every such merge, report to the owner what was merged. When something needs a decision or a coordinated fix, do not merge: report it or follow the fix path.
- Open PR hygiene (lead): no open PR without an owner and a next step; ask the same day if blocked.
## Testing
- Locally: only tests for the touched area. After deploy: affected flows vs criteria + short smoke. Full regression only before a release or after wide changes (auth, routing, migrations).
## Servers
- Read logs/status freely. Any change, manual deploy or rollback: owner approval, back up configs first.
## Stop rule
- On «стоп»: finish or revert the current atomic step, leave clones clean, push nothing half-done, report branch/PR state, start nothing new.
